# Network Coprocessor Configuration
# This component wraps ESP-Hosted slave firmware. The gate below decides
# whether the wrapper compiles its slave-side SRCS (network_adapter
# example builds) or registers as an empty component (host-side
# examples that pull network_coprocessor transitively via webrtc_bridge).

menu "Network Coprocessor (slave-side firmware)"

config NETWORK_COPROCESSOR_BUILD_FIRMWARE
    bool "Build network_coprocessor as the SDIO/SPI slave firmware"
    default n
    help
        Enable when this build IS the co-processor slave firmware
        (e.g. examples/network_adapter on ESP32-C5/C6). The wrapper
        then compiles esp_hosted/slave/main/*.c — including slave_bt.c
        and the slave_*_api transport files — and exposes the
        host_power_save API used by signaling_only's power-save hooks.

        Keep disabled (default) for host-side single-device builds
        (webrtc_classic, esp_camera, signaling_only as a standalone)
        so the slave-side firmware doesn't get linked into the host
        image where it would reference esp_vhci_host_* HCI symbols
        that aren't built into a host-side BT stack.

endmenu

# Pull in the complete slave Kconfig from the esp_hosted submodule.
# All the CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_* knobs it defines are referenced by the
# wrapper's slave-side CMakeLists when
# CONFIG_NETWORK_COPROCESSOR_BUILD_FIRMWARE=y.
rsource "../esp_hosted/slave/main/Kconfig.projbuild"
